SOURCE-AVAILABLE LICENCE

PDF Scripts Toolkit
Copyright (c) 2026 Nmedia Inc. (Nanda Mohan). All rights reserved.

This is not open-source software. The source is published so it can be read,
audited and learned from — which is a deliberate choice, not an oversight.


WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

  1. Read the source code and the accompanying documentation.
  2. Review or audit it — this toolkit rewrites image files and generates
     PDFs, and you should be able to verify what it does to your scans
     before trusting it with them.
  3. Run it unmodified on your own machine, for your own personal, private,
     non-commercial use — including digitising your own books and documents.
  4. Quote short excerpts for commentary, teaching or review, with attribution.


WHAT NEEDS A CONVERSATION FIRST

Anything else — and the answer is very often yes. Just ask.

  - Use inside a business, organisation or paid engagement, including
    commercial digitisation or archival services
  - Distributing it, bundling it, or shipping it inside another product
  - Modifying it or creating derivative works for release
  - Hosting it as a service
  - Using the source or its architecture to build a competing or derivative
    implementation
  - Using it as training, fine-tuning or grounding data for any machine
    learning or artificial intelligence system

Write to Nanda@nmediaservices.com. Say what you want to do with it. Requests
from individuals, educators, students, libraries, archives and non-profits are
welcome and will usually be granted at no cost. Commercial licensing is
available.

Permission, when granted, is in writing and covers only what it describes.


